  ('PHY 154', 'General Physics for Physical Sciences III', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Geology', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Elective.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Department of Statistics undergraduate course module'),
  ('CHM 112', 'Basic Principles of Physical Chemistry', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Geology', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Gas Laws and Kinetic Theory: Kinetic theory of gases, elementary derivation and deduction of gas laws, molecular speeds, deviations from ideal behaviour, van der Waals modification, and gas liquefaction. Phase Equilibrium and Solutions: Phase transitions and phase equilibria in one-component systems. Ideal solutions, Raoult''s law, Henry''s law, real solutions, and colligative properties -- vapour pressure lowering, boiling point elevation, freezing point lowering, osmotic pressure. Thermodynamics and Kinetics: Aspects of the first law of thermodynamics, thermochemistry, entropy, free energy, and spontaneous changes. Ionic equilibria, acids, bases, indicators, and buffers. Elementary chemical kinetics, factors affecting reaction rates, rate laws, order and molecularity, zero and first order reactions, Arrhenius equation, and collision and transition state theories.', '["Gas Laws and Kinetic Theory: Kinetic theory of gases, elementary derivation and deduction of gas laws, molecular speeds, deviations from ideal behaviour, van der Waals modification, and gas liquefaction", "Phase Equilibrium and Solutions: Phase transitions and phase equilibria in one-component systems. Ideal solutions, Raoult''s law, Henry''s law, real solutions, and colligative properties -- vapour pressure lowering, boiling point elevation, freezing point lowering, osmotic pressure", "Thermodynamics and Kinetics: Aspects of the first law of thermodynamics, thermochemistry, entropy, free energy, and spontaneous changes. Ionic equilibria, acids, bases, indicators, and buffers. Elementary chemical kinetics, factors affecting reaction rates, rate laws, order and molecularity, zero and first order reactions, Arrhenius equation, and collision and transition state theories"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Physical Sciences course catalogue (2014/2015)'),
  ('CHM 122', 'Basic Principles of Organic Chemistry', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Geology', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Structure and Classification: Historical survey of organic chemistry, IUPAC nomenclature, classification of organic compounds, homologous series, elemental analysis, molecular formulas, and structural isomerism. Bonding and Reactivity: Isolation and purification methods, functional group concepts, resonance, and aromaticity. Electronic theory in organic chemistry. Functional Groups: Brief study of saturated and unsaturated hydrocarbons, cyclic hydrocarbons, alcohols, alkyl halides, ethers, aldehydes, ketones, carboxylic acids, amines, and aromatic compounds. Comparison of phenols and aryl halides. Stereochemistry and Lipids: Introduction to oils, fats, and stereoisomerism.', '["Structure and Classification: Historical survey of organic chemistry, IUPAC nomenclature, classification of organic compounds, homologous series, elemental analysis, molecular formulas, and structural isomerism", "Bonding and Reactivity: Isolation and purification methods, functional group concepts, resonance, and aromaticity. Electronic theory in organic chemistry", "Functional Groups: Brief study of saturated and unsaturated hydrocarbons, cyclic hydrocarbons, alcohols, alkyl halides, ethers, aldehydes, ketones, carboxylic acids, amines, and aromatic compounds. Comparison of phenols and aryl halides", "Stereochemistry and Lipids: Introduction to oils, fats, and stereoisomerism"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Physical Sciences course catalogue (2014/2015)'),
  ('BIO 152', 'General Biology II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Geology', '100 Level', 'second', 3, 'Elective.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Department of Statistics undergraduate course module'),
  ('GSP 102', 'The Use of English II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Geology', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Part A: Basic Grammar: Introduction. The concept of grammar and its place in language teaching and learning. Parts of speech and their functions (treated in detail). Closed and open class items in parts of speech, Nominalization, Grammatical Structures: the phrase, the clause and the sentence. Elementary Clause Analysis, Sentence Types, Elements and Patterns. Agreement (Grammatical agreement, Notional agreement, Proximity agreement) Agreement with the correlatives. Direct and Reported Speech, Error typology identification and correction.

Part B: Varieties of writing. Introduction (The Meaning, Nature and Purpose of Writing, Writing Types or Genres and their Characteristics). The paragraph as the basic unit of an essay (Types, Development of the Paragraph, Methods of Paragraph Development, The thesis statement). Point of view and style in writing. Qualities of a good piece of writing: Form, Diction and Content in writing. The Mechanics of Writing: punctuation, spelling and capitalization.

Part C: Writing Genres - Planning and choosing your theme. Deciding your genre. Choosing and developing your plot. Point of view, setting and characterization. Using the language that works. Essay Writing — Narration, Description, Exposition and Argumentation. Technical Writing: Letter Writing, Memorandum Writing, Speech Writing, Agenda and Minutes, own story for practice, Computer-linked writing, types, style, language, and process.', '["Part A: Basic Grammar - The concept of grammar, Parts of speech, Grammatical Structures, Sentence Types, Agreement, Direct and Reported Speech, Error typology", "Part B: Varieties of writing - Meaning, Nature and Purpose of Writing, the paragraph as the basic unit of an essay, the thesis statement, Qualities of a good piece of writing, Mechanics of Writing", "Part C: Writing Genres - Planning and choosing your theme, plot, point of view, setting and characterization", "Essay Writing - Narration, Description, Exposition and Argumentation", "Technical Writing - Letter Writing, Memorandum Writing, Speech Writing, Agenda and Minutes"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Mechanical Engineering handbook'),
  ('FRE 102', 'Elementary French II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Geology', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Elective.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Physical Sciences course catalogue (2014/2015)'),
  ('MTH 122', 'Elementary Mathematics III', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Geology', '100 Level', 'second', 3, 'Elective. Geometric representation of vectors in 1-3 dimensions, Components, direction cosines. Addition of vectors and multiplication of vectors by a scalar, linear independence. Scalar and vector products of two vectors. Differentiation and integration of vectors with respect to a scalar variable. Two-dimensional coordinate geometry. Straight lines, circles, parabolas, ellipses, hyperbolas. Tangents and normals. Kinematics of a particle. Components of velocity and acceleration of a particle moving in a plane. Force and momentum. Newton''s laws of motion; motion under gravity, projectile motion, resisted vertical motion of a particle, elastic string, motion of a simple pendulum, impulse and impact of momentum. Impact of two smooth elastic spheres. Direct and oblique impacts.', '["Geometric representation of vectors in 1-3 dimensions, Components, direction cosines", "Addition of vectors and multiplication of vectors by a scalar, linear independence", "Scalar and vector products of two vectors", "Differentiation and integration of vectors with respect to a scalar variable", "Two-dimensional coordinate geometry", "Straight lines, circles, parabolas, ellipses, hyperbolas", "Tangents and normals", "Kinematics of a particle", "Components of velocity and acceleration of a particle moving in a plane", "Force and momentum", "Newton''s laws of motion", "Motion under gravity, projectile motion, resisted vertical motion of a particle, elastic string, motion of a simple pendulum, impulse and impact of momentum", "Impact of two smooth elastic spheres", "Direct and oblique impacts"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Physical Sciences course catalogue (2014/2015)'),
  ('STA 203', 'Statistics for Physical Sciences and Engineering I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Geology', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'Initial steps in planning of biological experiments. Methods of data collection, presentation and analysis. Measures of central tendency and dispersion. Frequency distributions. Elementary probability. Discrete and continuous distributions: Binomial, Poisson, Normal and exponential distributions. Interval estimation.', '["Initial steps in planning of biological experiments", "Methods of data collection, presentation and analysis", "Measures of central tendency and dispersion", "Frequency distributions", "Elementary probability", "Discrete and continuous distributions: Binomial, Poisson, Normal and exponential distributions", "Interval estimation"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Physical Sciences course catalogue (2014/2015)'),
  ('CHM 171', 'Basic Practical Chemistry', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Geology', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'Laboratory Operations: Theory and practice of simple volumetric and quantitative analysis, simple organic preparations, functional group reactions, and physical chemistry determinations.', '["Laboratory Operations: Theory and practice of simple volumetric and quantitative analysis, simple organic preparations, functional group reactions, and physical chemistry determinations"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Physical Sciences course catalogue (2014/2015)'),
  ('CHM 211', 'General Physical Chemistry', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Geology', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'Gases and Thermodynamics: Molecular collisions in gases, virial equation, critical phenomena, and reduced properties. Chemical thermodynamics, detailed treatment of the first law of thermodynamics, and the Carnot cycle. Chemical Kinetics: Integrated rate equations for second and third order reactions, reaction mechanisms, rate laws, and the effect of temperature on reaction rates.

Prerequisite: CHM 112', '["Gases and Thermodynamics: Molecular collisions in gases, virial equation, critical phenomena, and reduced properties. Chemical thermodynamics, detailed treatment of the first law of thermodynamics, and the Carnot cycle", "Chemical Kinetics: Integrated rate equations for second and third order reactions, reaction mechanisms, rate laws, and the effect of temperature on reaction rates"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Physical Sciences course catalogue (2014/2015)'),
  ('COS 101', 'Introduction to Computer Science', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Geology', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'The programme table prints this course''s code as "SP 101" — a binding-fold scan artefact seen throughout this source; every other department''s programme table in the same document uses COS 101 for this exact title, so that code is used here. Concepts of hardware and software; basic subsystems of a digital computer; characteristics of a digital computer; devices/media; types/classes of computer emphasising the PC; history of computers and their generations. Problem-solving: algorithm, flowchart, pseudocode, program/data, running a program. Programming: introduction to Java/BASIC programming language syntax and programming. Booting and shutdown; types of operating system; user interface; managing information, computer malware (virus, etc); computer network; internet and web usage, e-mail, instant messaging, etc. Office applications; use of a statistical package and a database management system.', '["Concepts of hardware and software","basic subsystems of a digital computer","characteristics of a digital computer","devices/media","types/classes of computer emphasising the PC","history of computers and their generations","Problem-solving: algorithm, flowchart, pseudocode, program/data, running a program","Programming: introduction to Java/BASIC programming language syntax and programming","Booting and shutdown","types of operating system","user interface","managing information, computer malware (virus, etc)","computer network","internet and web usage, e-mail, instant messaging, etc","Office applications","use of a statistical package and a database management system"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Physical Sciences course catalogue (2014/2015)'),
